  "query_preview": "..\nThursday through Friday: The region is under a zonal flow \npattern with a strengthening ridge over the Southwest Conus and \na developing Gulf of Alaska Low. A weak wave will pass through \nthe region today but is only expected to bring isolated showers \nfor the Cascades and northern mountains. It will not bring much \nin the way of precip as probability of more than a hundredth are\nat most 20%. Winds will be light. Temperatures will continue to\nwarm through the period. Highs will be in the 70s to low 80s. \nClear sky and dry air will allow for lows to dip into the mid \n30s for the northern valleys. The range of lows will be mid 30s \nto 40s.\n\nSaturday through Wednesday: The ridge will build into the \nPacific Northwest behind the weak wave. It will continue the \ndry, warming trend through the end of the period. Weak waves \nwill continue to pass through the region but are not expected to\nbring much in the way of precip. It will bring a brief cool \ndown from the weekend. Nearly 80% of ensembles agree with this \npattern. The other 20% flatten the ridge with a stronger long \nwave trough pressing into the region on Tuesday. The dry, warm \nconditions return through the end of the week. Highs will be in \nthe 70s and low 80s. Lows will be in the upper 30s and low 50s. \nOvernight lows Looking ahead, next weekend is showing signs of \nbeing cooler with increased shower chances. /JDC",
